      "prose_no_unhedged_estimated_times": true,
      "prose_includes_any": ["06:00", "6:00", "6 AM", "6am", "6 am"]
    },
    "why": "The mirror of estimated-hours-must-be-hedged, and the reason the rule has to be conditional rather than 'never state a time'. This temple's hours ARE sourced (estimated.hours = false), so 06:00 may be stated precisely — prose_no_unhedged_estimated_times exempts it, and prose_includes_any requires it to actually survive into the text. Without this case, the honest fix for the other one is to hedge everything unconditionally, which throws away real sourced information and is its own dishonesty. Note prose_includes_any is the more brittle of the two assertions: it accepts several renderings of six o'clock, but a model that wrote 'at dawn' would fail it. That is intentional — losing a sourced value should be visible."
